# The rotation fold's cubins for RTX 5090 cards (pearl_rot_sm120w.cubin) that have mined on a card with every hit
# verified, one line for each:
#   <toolkit release> <hash>
# As pearl_rot_sm120.ref: probes/hand89/build_rot.py --arch sm_120w refuses to write the file unless what it built
# is listed here for the toolkit that built it, and the host loads it only when its hash is in kRotCubins
# (pearl_host_rot.inc). A line is added only after its file has run on an RTX 5090: probes/verify-hits.js 400 of
# 400 with the fold on.
#
# The 96 x 512 block (goal-nv50k): A shared by all eight warps, its stage ordered by the two groups' barriers
# (rfold.py w8=1 w8g=4, goal-nvk22's protocol), the rest of sm_120's keys. pearl_rot.cu built with -DROT_W8=1 and a
# base that has eight barriers (-DROT_C=49155). The host takes it on cards of compute 12.0 with 128 SMs or more
# (RTX 5090s), which mine at their power cap; other RTX 50 cards take pearl_rot_sm120.cubin.

# CUDA 13.3, build_rot.py --arch sm_120w on two Salad PCs' Linux and on Windows: the same hash. verify-hits 400 of
# 400 on two 575 W RTX 5090s (drivers 610.88 and 621.01: 931 and 940 hits). hashrate.js, four 120 s legs each
# against pearl_rot_sm120.cubin's keys on the same PC: 434.96 against 432.59 (+0.55%) and 438.30 against 431.83
# (+1.50%) (tuning/benchmark.md, 13 November).
# goal-nv50q (14 November): the same with the transcript word loaded a chunk early and no sixth gather quad
# (rfold.py trl=1 cq=0). verify-hits 400 of 400 on two capped 5090s; +1.6% and +1.0% against the file before
# (9da716e2) on two 575 W PCs (tuning/benchmark.md).
